  "note": "Urban council election, 21 May 1958. Eight nominations were received for nine seats, so there was no poll; Dr. H. L. Donnan, who did not seek re-election, was deemed re-elected with the retiring members, and the eight nominees were returned unopposed. Mr. W. M. Dunn was the outgoing Mayor. The two new members were Col. D. C. M'Cormick and Lieut.-Col. V. Onsworth. Returned unopposed."
